;; The road from spawn to a dead Ender Dragon, as the results page draws it (bb site, issue #116).
;; The race's own chain comes from goals.edn up to ci/race.edn's :race/until (page/chain), so it
;; follows the bot; this file adds what the races do not play yet, in the order the game forces
;; (issue #10): the goal rows that exist only as asides (proven, if at all, in a gym), then the
;; stages no goal row plays yet. When the race is raised past a stage, the chain takes it over and
;; its line here is ignored. Each stage says in a few words what done means, its phase (the page
;; colours and groups by it) and the roadmap issue that carries it.
{:road/after [:blaze-rods :ender-pearls :eyes-of-ender :eye-throw :stronghold :portal-room]
 :road/unbuilt [{:id :end-portal :issue 266 :says "twelve eyes in the frames: the end portal lit"}
                {:id :the-end :issue 266 :says "through the end portal, standing in the End"}
                {:id :dragon :issue 267 :says "crystals broken, the dragon killed: the win"}]
 :road/phases {:wood :wood
               :kit :wood
               :pickaxe :wood
               :cobblestone :stone
               :stone-pickaxe :stone
               :furnace :stone
               :ingots :iron
               :bucket :iron
               :water-bucket :iron
               :flint-and-steel :iron
               :iron-kit :iron
               :portal-kit :portal
               :gear :portal
               :cast-one :portal
               :portal :portal
               :nether :nether
               :fortress :nether
               :blaze-rods :nether
               :ender-pearls :stronghold
               :eyes-of-ender :stronghold
               :eye-throw :stronghold
               :stronghold :stronghold
               :portal-room :stronghold
               :end-portal :end
               :the-end :end
               :dragon :end}
